{
  "_readme": "Fixture for the two contrast bands of WCAG 1.4.3. Primitives hold six neutral greys (r = g = b) and one font-size FLOAT; Semantic holds three text roles and one background, each with a Light and a Dark value. color/text/primary passes everywhere, color/text/secondary sits between 3:1 and 4.5:1 in both modes (passes only as large text), and color/text/muted sits below 3:1 in both modes. Scopes, codeSyntax.WEB names, modes, pages and the text-style binding are complete, so the only findings are the contrast pairs under test.",
